# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents (kept out of the shared `AGENTS.md` since T3 Code is
developed in many places). They cover the pre-provisioned VM environment and non-obvious run caveats.

## Toolchain

The Cloud Agent image provides Node 24.21.0 (`engines.node` is `^24.13.1`), the global `vp` (Vite+)
CLI with bundled pnpm 11.10.0, and Rust stable (edition 2024 for `native/resource-monitor`).
`libsecret-1-dev` and `pkg-config` are installed for the Linux desktop secret helper.

- `node`, `npm`, and `npx` on `PATH` are Node 24.21.0 via symlinks in `/usr/local/cargo/bin`, which
  is ahead of `/exec-daemon/node` (Node 22.14.0). Calling `/exec-daemon/node` directly is still Node 22.
  The nvm install lives at `$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0`.
- `vp` is `/usr/local/bin/vp`. Use it as the package manager and task runner (`vp i`, `vp check`,
  `vp run typecheck`, `vp test`, `vp run --filter <pkg> <script>`).
- `vp check` also runs the formatter (not just lint); markdown edits must be formatter-clean. Run
  `vp check --fix` before committing.

## Running the web app

- `vp run dev` (from repo root; `npm run dev` is the same script) starts contracts (watch), web
  (Vite, port 5733), and the server (`node --watch`, port 13773). Use `vp run dev:server` /
  `vp run dev:web` for one side. If base ports are taken it auto-offsets to the next free pair, so
  read the actual ports from stdout. Avoid production `build`/`start` in dev.
- Browser dev is single-origin. Leave `VITE_HTTP_URL` and `VITE_WS_URL` unset; the dev runner deletes
  them and sets `T3CODE_SINGLE_ORIGIN_DEV=1` so Vite proxies `/api` and `/ws`.
- Vite listens on IPv6 `localhost` (`::1`). Open `http://localhost:5733`. `http://127.0.0.1:5733`
  is connection refused. The server process listens on `127.0.0.1`.
- Auth/pairing: the server prints a pairing URL to stdout on startup
  (e.g. `http://localhost:5733/pair#token=XXXX`). Open that URL in the browser to pair before the web
  UI can talk to the server. For an isolated run, pass `--home-dir` (a worktree's gitignored `.t3`,
  or an explicit directory). The main checkout otherwise uses `~/.t3/dev`. Never point a server at
  `~/.t3/userdata`.
- Agent providers are external CLIs (`codex`, `claude`, `cursor-agent`, `opencode`) probed on `PATH`.
  Without one installed the UI loads but no agent can run. Claude Code
  (`npm i -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code`) works headlessly using `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from the
  environment (the server forwards `process.env` to the child; no interactive `claude auth login`
  needed). Provider probing runs at startup and refreshes roughly every 5 minutes — restart the dev
  server to pick up a newly installed provider CLI immediately.

## Mobile native builds

This environment does not include the Android SDK, a JDK 17 `JAVA_HOME`, or an Android emulator.
The VM has no `/dev/kvm`, so a hardware-accelerated emulator cannot run. iOS builds need macOS.
Use EAS (`vp run eas:android:*`) or a machine with the native toolchain for device builds. Web and
server development, `vp test`, and `vp run lint:mobile` do not need that toolchain.

## Known flaky tests (unrelated to setup)

- `apps/server/src/git/GitManager.test.ts` (cross-repo PR metadata, can time out at 12s).
- `apps/server/src/provider/Layers/ProviderRegistry.test.ts` (codex binaryPath re-probe ordering).
